LOCAL EVIDENCE-FINALIZATION NOTE

The first post-edit secret-scan shell invocation did not start because its
credential-pattern quoting was syntactically invalid. It exited before scanning
or changing any file and emitted no matched content. The scan was repeated with
a fixed literal pattern and its aggregate result is the authoritative result.

The first read-only Tailscale server-discovery wrapper was rejected before
execution because it included a temporary-file removal command. No connection
or mutation occurred. Discovery was repeated without a temporary file.

The replacement read-only discovery initially reported no eligible target
because its probe required the Control path and a guessed Application checkout
name. The online Linux peer and VPN were green; the exact Control-only path
probe then succeeded with the existing non-interactive SSH identity. No address
or identity was emitted and no server mutation occurred.

The first stage-check wrapper reused zsh's reserved `status` variable and
aborted before its VPN query. It was corrected with task-specific variable
names; no connection or mutation occurred.
